<div class="page-wrapper">
    <div class="dark-box"></div>
    <div class="content">
        <h1 id="introduction">Introduction</h1>
<p>Web storefront, mobile app and admin APIs for AANI GEMAS.</p>
<aside>
    <strong>Base URL</strong>: <code>http://localhost:8000</code>
</aside>
<pre><code>AANI GEMAS backend API (v1). Groups are prefixed by platform:

* **Web** – `/api/v1/web/*` (storefront)
* **Mobile** – `/api/v1/mobile/*` (same behaviour as web, plus `app` in bootstrap, PaymentSheet keys at checkout and push-token endpoints)
* **Admin** – `/api/v1/admin/*` (admin SPA, session cookie)
* **Webhooks** – `/api/v1/webhooks/stripe`

Conventions:

* Money is always `{ "amount": 82137, "currency": "EUR", "formatted": "€821.37" }` (`amount` in minor units).
* Send `X-Currency: EUR|USD|INR|AED|GBP` to get prices in that currency; `meta.currency` says which one was used.
* Lists return `{ data, meta, links }` (`per_page` max 50). Validation errors return 422 `{ message, errors }` with user-friendly messages.
* Customer endpoints use `Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;` from register / login / Google.
* The server prices everything: clients send only ids, qty, size and codes.</code></pre>

        <h1 id="authenticating-requests">Authenticating requests</h1>
<p>To authenticate requests, include an <strong><code>Authorization</code></strong> header with the value <strong><code>"Bearer {YOUR_TOKEN}"</code></strong>.</p>
<p>All authenticated endpoints are marked with a <code>requires authentication</code> badge in the documentation below.</p>
<p>Get a customer token from <code>POST /auth/login</code>, <code>/auth/register</code> or <code>/auth/google</code> and send it as <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code>.</p>

        <h1 id="web-store">Web · Store</h1>

    <p>Public store data: bootstrap and home. Send <code>X-Currency</code> (EUR, USD, INR, AED, GBP) to get prices in that currency.</p>

                                <h2 id="web-store-GETapi-v1-web-bootstrap">Bootstrap</h2>

<p>
</p>

<p>Everything the app needs on start: brand, navigation, footer, contact, currencies (with rates), tax,
free-shipping threshold, shipping methods, countries, order stages, catalog filters, Stripe publishable key,
Google client id, gold rate. The mobile variant also returns <code>app</code> (versions, force update, maintenance).</p>

<span id="example-requests-GETapi-v1-web-bootstrap">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/web/bootstrap" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --header "X-Currency: EUR"</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/web/bootstrap"
);

const headers = {
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
    "X-Currency": "EUR",
};


fetch(url, {
