                <h1 id="mobile-checkout-orders">Mobile · Checkout & orders</h1>

    

                                <h2 id="mobile-checkout-orders-POSTapi-v1-mobile-checkout">Checkout</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Requires an <code>Idempotency-Key</code> header (e.g. a UUID per checkout attempt; repeating the same request
with the same key returns the same order). The server re-quotes the cart, validates stock, sizes and
combos, creates a <code>pending_payment</code> order with snapshots and a Stripe PaymentIntent in the order currency.
Web returns <code>payment: {client_secret, publishable_key}</code>; mobile also returns <code>customer_id</code> and
<code>ephemeral_key</code> for PaymentSheet. Then confirm with Stripe and poll <code>GET /orders/{number}</code>.</p>

<span id="example-requests-POSTapi-v1-mobile-checkout">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request POST \
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/mobile/checkout" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Idempotency-Key: 6f1c2b8e-3d4a-4c6f-9a1b-2e3f4a5b6c7d" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --header "X-Currency: EUR" \
    --data "{
    \"items\": [
        {
            \"type\": \"product\",
            \"product_id\": 7,
            \"qty\": 1
        }
    ],
    \"address_id\": 1,
    \"address\": [],
    \"save_address\": false,
    \"shipping_method\": \"standard\",
    \"coupon_code\": \"AANI10\",
    \"customer_note\": \"Gift wrap please\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/mobile/checkout"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_TOKEN}",
    "Idempotency-Key": "6f1c2b8e-3d4a-4c6f-9a1b-2e3f4a5b6c7d",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
    "X-Currency": "EUR",
};

let body = {
    "items": [
        {
            "type": "product",
            "product_id": 7,
            "qty": 1
        }
    ],
    "address_id": 1,
    "address": [],
    "save_address": false,
    "shipping_method": "standard",
    "coupon_code": "AANI10",
    "customer_note": "Gift wrap please"
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

</span>

